  "worked_solution": "First, we decompose all of the terms into their various factors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{yz}{3xz}=\\frac{y\\cdot z}{3\\cdot x\\cdot z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel out all the pairs of common factors in the numerator and denominator. In this case, there is one pair of $z$'s.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\cdot z}{3\\cdot x\\cdot z} & = \\\\ \\frac{y\\cdot \\cancel{z}}{3\\cdot x\\cdot \\cancel{z}} & = \\\\ \\frac{y}{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\frac{y}{3x}.$",
